{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-song-of-solomon-008",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 8,
  "title": "Song of Solomon 8",
  "display_title": "Song of Solomon 8",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "song-of-solomon",
  "book": "Song of Solomon",
  "bookName": "Song of Solomon",
  "bookOrder": 22,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 8,
  "sortOrder": 22008,
  "verseCount": 14,
  "aliases": [
    "Song",
    "Song of Songs",
    "SOS",
    "Canticles"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "O that thou wert as my brother, that sucked the breasts of my mother! when I should find thee without, I would kiss thee; yea, I should not be despised.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "I would lead thee, and bring thee into my mother’s house, who would instruct me: I would cause thee to drink of spiced wine of the juice of my pomegranate.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "His left hand should be under my head, and his right hand should embrace me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "I charge you, O daughters of Jerusalem, that ye stir not up, nor awake my love, until he please.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Who is this that cometh up from the wilderness, leaning upon her beloved? I raised thee up under the apple tree: there thy mother brought thee forth: there she brought thee forth that bare thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Set me as a seal upon thine heart, as a seal upon thine arm: for love is strong as death; jealousy is cruel as the grave: the coals thereof are coals of fire, which hath a most vehement flame.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Many waters cannot quench love, neither can the floods drown it: if a man would give all the substance of his house for love, it would utterly be contemned.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "We have a little sister, and she hath no breasts: what shall we do for our sister in the day when she shall be spoken for?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "If she be a wall, we will build upon her a palace of silver: and if she be a door, we will inclose her with boards of cedar.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "I am a wall, and my breasts like towers: then was I in his eyes as one that found favour.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Solomon had a vineyard at Baalhamon; he let out the vineyard unto keepers; every one for the fruit thereof was to bring a thousand pieces of silver.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "My vineyard, which is mine, is before me: thou, O Solomon, must have a thousand, and those that keep the fruit thereof two hundred.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Thou that dwellest in the gardens, the companions hearken to thy voice: cause me to hear it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Make haste, my beloved, and be thou like to a roe or to a young hart upon the mountains of spices.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 8:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:8:14"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
